HTTP/2 SETTINGS: align the receive buffer that Vect is overlaid on

AWS.HTTP2.Frame.Settings.Read reads the frame payload into Data, a
Stream_Element_Array (alignment 1), and then overlays the array Vect (of
Payload, alignment 2 or 4) on it with an Address clause.  On targets that need
strict alignment (32-bit ARM) GNAT warns:

  warning: specified address for "Vect" may be inconsistent with alignment
  warning: program execution may be erroneous (RM 13.3(27))
  warning: alignment of "Vect" is 2
  warning: alignment of "Data" is 1

which is fatal in AWS' debug profile (-gnatwe), and is a real problem: nothing
guarantees the stack slot of Data is aligned for Payload.

Give Data the maximum alignment so that the overlay is valid.

--- a/src/http2/aws-http2-frame-settings.adb
+++ b/src/http2/aws-http2-frame-settings.adb
@@ -114,7 +114,9 @@
       Size : Stream_Element_Count :=
                Stream_Element_Count (Len) / (Payload'Size / 8);
       Idx  : Stream_Element_Count := 1;
-      Data : Stream_Element_Array (1 .. Stream_Element_Count (Len));
+      Data : Stream_Element_Array (1 .. Stream_Element_Count (Len))
+        with Alignment => Standard'Maximum_Alignment;
+      --  Vect is overlaid on Data, so Data must be aligned for Payload
       Vect : Set (1 .. Size);
       for Vect'Address use Data'Address;
       Head : Frame.Object;
